WHAT: guard the seven setAccessibleName()/setAccessibleDescription() calls in
      KContextualHelpButton, KMessageWidget and KPasswordDialog on
      QT_CONFIG(accessibility).
WHY:  QT_FEATURE_accessibility is -1 in wk qtbase (qtgui-config.h), and
      qwidget.h declares those two setters INSIDE `#if QT_CONFIG(accessibility)`
      -- so the failure reads as "no member named setAccessibleName in
      KContextualHelpButton", which points at the subclass rather than at the
      feature. There is no AT-SPI bus, no UIAutomation and no VoiceOver behind
      a wk node surface for the strings to reach. Every one of them exists
      solely to be spoken by a screen reader, so nothing a sighted user can
      observe changes. If wk ever grows an accessibility bridge, these guards
      are the first thing to delete.
UPSTREAM: as-is. QT_CONFIG(accessibility) is a legitimate Qt configuration and
      guarding for it is a plain portability fix.
diff --git a/src/kcontextualhelpbutton.cpp b/src/kcontextualhelpbutton.cpp
index c462437..db74e66 100644
--- a/src/kcontextualhelpbutton.cpp
+++ b/src/kcontextualhelpbutton.cpp
@@ -65,7 +65,9 @@ KContextualHelpButtonPrivate::KContextualHelpButtonPrivate(KContextualHelpButton
     // interface. Usually we start button labels with a verb, however the help text contained within this button will automatically be read by the screen
     // reader without requiring additional user input. In this sense the label here is more of an announcement that the text read afterwards is help relevant
     // to the current context.
+#if QT_CONFIG(accessibility)
     q_ptr->setAccessibleName(QObject::tr("Contextual Help", "@action:button accessible name"));
+#endif
     q_ptr->setAttribute(Qt::WidgetAttribute::WA_CustomWhatsThis); // Makes sure clicking this button in whatsThisMode triggers it instead of doing nothing.
 
     auto popup = new QWidgetAction{q_ptr};
@@ -94,7 +96,9 @@ void KContextualHelpButtonPrivate::setContextualHelpText(const QString &contextu
         return;
     }
     q_ptr->setToolTip(contextualHelpText);
+#if QT_CONFIG(accessibility)
     q_ptr->setAccessibleDescription(QTextDocumentFragment::fromHtml(contextualHelpText).toPlainText()); // Makes sure html tags aren't read out.
+#endif
     m_popupLabel->setText(contextualHelpText);
     Q_EMIT q_ptr->contextualHelpTextChanged(contextualHelpText);
 }
